title: 'EPMB: determine the signed base deposit at registration'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The base deposit of a signed submission is now charged once, when the submitter calls
    `register`, and stored in the submission metadata as `base`. On every `submit_page`, the held
    deposit becomes that base plus the per-page deposit of the stored pages. Previously, every
    `submit_page` re-computed the whole deposit from the current queue length, so the held amount
    depended on registrations made by other accounts after the submitter registered. That
    re-computation also counted the submitter itself, so a submitter that stored pages held the
    base one step of `DepositBase` higher than at registration. The base now stays at the
    registration price.

    `CalculatePageDeposit::calculate_page_deposit` no longer takes the number of existing
    submitters. Custom implementations must drop that argument.

    The signed pallet now has storage version 1. Runtimes must include
    `pallet_election_provider_multi_block::signed::migrations::v1::MigrateV0ToV1` in their
    migrations. It adds `base` to every stored submission: the held deposit minus the per-page
    deposit of the stored pages, at the current price. For accounts in `Invulnerables`, the whole
    deposit becomes the base. The base is at least the lowest base deposit for the account's
    current status, and at most the held deposit. If `DepositPerPage` changes in the same release,
    the derived base absorbs the per-page price difference on stored pages for the rest of that
    round.
crates:
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-block
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
